  "reply": {
    "analysis_type": "paradigm_network",
    "rationale": "Two small paradigms are defensible. First, CCL and FCL form an exact compositional minimal pair in the shared frame _CL: C=‘cool’ vs F=‘folded’, with CL=‘cloth’. Second, six codes share the frame _R10 with coherent root substitution: BDR10, CL2ER10, FCR10, SSR10, T6R10, WSR10. Across these, R10 contributes a stable right-face + 10-seconds specification, while the initial fillers contribute the differing procedure/material meanings. I reject a broader CC family and the suggested FC family: the available longer CC... symbols do not yet support a clean shared compositional slot analysis, and FC is not independently supported as a stable morpheme across FCL and FCR10. All other symbols are left lexical to avoid over-segmentation.",
